# SaaS Foundation Implementation Plan

## Goal
Transition Superactive from a single-tenant, file-based prototype to a multi-tenant, database-backed SaaS application ready for Phase 4 (Dashboard).

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database**: We are using SQLite (`aiosqlite`) for the MVP. Migration to PostgreSQL is designed to be a simple driver swap later.
> **Auth**: JWT-based authentication is now enforced on all API routes except telephony webhooks (Twilio).
> **Data Migration**: On first startup, existing JSON files in `agents/` and `data/` will be imported into the DB automatically.

## Architecture Guidelines
- **Tenant Isolation**: Every database table (except Tenants itself) has a `tenant_id` column. API routes strictly filter by `request.user.tenant_id`.
- **Async First**: All database I/O is asynchronous to prevent blocking the event loop during voice processing.
- **Telephony Handling**: Twilio webhooks remain public but are secured by internal logic (validating Agent ID exists).

